# Pinned inputs for the test-VM image. remote.sh refuses to build unless both
# image values are real name@sha256:<64 hex> references, the Slack spec is an
# exact @openclaw/slack@<version>, and its integrity is a real sha512 (no placeholders).
# Plain KEY=VALUE lines only; remote.sh parses them, it does not source them.
#
# Official OpenClaw release 2026.10.5 (multi-arch index; the plugin needs
# openclaw >=2026.10.5). Resolved 2026-11-11 from ghcr.io (anonymous token,
# HEAD /v2/openclaw/openclaw/manifests/2026.10.5). The 2026.10.5-slim tag
# resolves to the same index. Runtime user in the image config: node (uid 1000).
OPENCLAW_IMAGE=ghcr.io/openclaw/openclaw@sha256:f40d1e66fd14d8c5b49c832f4100f83b53fdc01f5108f7db11de38fd0ee6dbe5
#
# Google Cloud CLI 593.0.0-stable (Debian image; SDK at /usr/lib/google-cloud-sdk).
# Resolved 2026-11-11 from gcr.io for the same tag (also what `stable` points at).
SDK_IMAGE=gcr.io/google.com/cloudsdktool/google-cloud-cli@sha256:54e711173abf8aebf025d0a20815088bfb6ab627eae39d8d0ab6df6ec114cbf6
#
# Slack ships outside the official image (its package sets bundledDist:false), so
# the build downloads this exact package with `npm pack` and fails unless the file
# matches the registry's dist.integrity below (resolved 2026-11-11 from
# registry.npmjs.org for @openclaw/slack@2026.10.5). apply.mjs installs that local
# tarball after applying the PR #34 navigation backport. Keep the version equal
# to the OpenClaw release above.
# The codex plugin is bundled in the official image (docs/install/docker.md), so it
# is neither downloaded nor installed here; apply.mjs fails if it is missing.
SLACK_PLUGIN_SPEC=@openclaw/slack@2026.10.5
SLACK_PLUGIN_INTEGRITY=sha512-AzWaSLfUQZWPwDdrLXzXeQ/AraXPEnkTTWKTKq4MFO39futFAxy+FulsYSStDYEd1B0YjtWGvXswBjdrmwRlBw==
